From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:08:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the tasks card's Open turns into Back, and the
 eye's content sits on the panel

Two operator asks of 2026-11-22 on the tasks card.

Open Thread at This Task (0041, 0120) brought a subagent's thread on
screen and stayed an open-arrow there, so the way back was the thread's
own navigation. While the task's thread is the one its conversation
shows, the row's button now reads "Back to the Main Thread", with the
Exit icon, and brings the main thread back:
- HeldView keeps shown_session, the session of the thread the view shows
  (its root's, or a subagent's it navigated to). The card already
  observes each held view; refresh_view now updates shown_session before
  its root check, since navigating to a child changes the view without
  changing its root, and notifies when it moves.
- The row's task thread is the AcpSubagent source's child, or the feed
  task's child_session_id. shows_task_thread matches it against the view
  holding the row's session, so only that row goes back.
- TasksCardEvent::ReturnToMainThread { session_id }: the panel brings the
  conversation forward (open_thread_by_session) and navigates it to its
  main thread (navigate_to_thread), logging the step.

Watch This Task (0094): the preview drew its output and a shell's tail on
the editor's background and a fallback body on the card's elevated
surface. What the eye shows now always sits on the agent panel's
background (preview::watch_background, panel_background). render_tail,
render_result_line and render_expanded_body take the background, so the
chevron's details keep the editor's.

Tests: tasks_card::back_to_main_thread, 2 GPUI on the native-subagent
rig -- Open shows the child and the same button then reads Back and
returns to the main thread; on Bravo's thread only Bravo's row goes back,
Alpha's still opens. Red seen with shows_task_thread forced false: both
failed. The background has no automated test (GPUI tests do not expose a
painted colour); it is proved on Xvfb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
